00:03:24,574 --> 00:03:26,930
as before because I'm all running this

78
00:03:26,962 --> 00:03:30,249
locally so sending that request is super

79
00:03:30,249 --> 00:03:33,648
fast but actually the input is only cleared

80
00:03:33,856 --> 00:03:37,688
after the goal was sent and the response was

81
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,297
received.

82
00:03:39,068 --> 00:03:42,504
Now listening to HTMX events like this is

83
00:03:42,777 --> 00:03:45,859
possible, but we can actually write less

84
00:03:45,972 --> 00:03:46,421
code here.

85
00:03:47,658 --> 00:03:49,890
Because for example, whenever you're using

86
00:03:50,066 --> 00:03:53,053
hx:on to listen to HTMX events,

87
00:03:53,679 --> 00:03:54,803
you can omit this

88
00:03:55,381 --> 00:03:59,122
HTMX colon part, which is part of all those

89
00:03:59,299 --> 00:04:00,487
HTMX event names,

90
00:04:01,467 --> 00:04:03,458
and you can instead write a double colon

91
00:04:03,474 --> 00:04:03,586
here.

92
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:07,266
This is simply a shortcut, a shorter

93
00:04:07,266 --> 00:04:10,815
notation that's understood by HTMX that

94
00:04:10,848 --> 00:04:14,435
tells HTMX that the event name thereafter is

95
00:04:14,709 --> 00:04:17,995
an HTMX event and should be preceded with

96
00:04:18,188 --> 00:04:19,202
